---
title: Our process
description: 'How We Build Scalable Data Platforms:  We design and implement modular data platforms that are flexible, efficient, and built to scale.'
hero:
  title: Restore Predictability to Your Data Platforms
  subtitle: |-
    Your team should be delivering new capabilities, not spending its time managing unstable deployments, recurring incidents, and operational complexity. 

    We help data teams introduce the engineering structure that their platforms are missing.
  button_text: Learn more about how we work
  button_target: /contact/
  image: ./src/assets/images/backgrounds/sfondi-dyvenia23.jpg
intro:
  title1: What Happens When
  title2: Complexity Outpaces Structure?
  content: |-
    Pipelines multiply, ownership becomes unclear, deployments become harder to manage, and monitoring becomes inconsistent.

    The platform still works, but **nobody fully trusts it**.
what_are:
  title: A Structured Path Back to Control
  content: |-
    Regaining control doesn’t require a complete rebuild. 

    It requires identifying where operational predictability breaks down, validating improvements with measurable results, and implementing them at scale.

    That’s the process we follow.
  button_text: Explore Our Process
  button_target: /contact/
  image: /assets/images/Modular_Data_Platform.png
  image_alt: Data platform architecture schema with tools and technologies
steps:
  title: Our Process
  intro: We follow a structured, two-phase approach to help data teams regain control of their platforms and scale with confidence.
  title_outcomes: 'Outcomes:'
  title_what: What do we do?
steps_elements:
  stage_1:
    label: Phase 1
    name: Identify & Validate
    steps:
      - label: Step 1
        title: Assessment
        content: We evaluate your platform, operating model, and delivery processes to identify the highest-impact opportunities for improvement.
        outcomes: |-
          - Quantified optimization opportunities
          - Clear visibility into risks and bottlenecks
          - Prioritized recommendations based on business impact
          - A focused scope for the proof of concept
      - label: Step 2
        title: Proof of Concept
        content: We implement and validate a focus improvement in a controlled scope to demonstrate measurable operational impact.
        outcomes: |-
          - Measurable reduction in cost, risk, or operational overhead
          - A scalable technical approach validated in practice
          - Faster and safer deployment workflows
          - Evidence-based justification for broader implementation
  stage_2:
    label: Phase 2
    name: Scale & Operate
    steps:
      - label: Step 3
        title: Implementation
        content: We roll out the validated improvements across your platform using production-grade engineering practices.
        outcomes: |-
          - A stable and scalable platform foundation
          - Reliable deployment and execution processes
          - Improved observability and operational visibility
          - Optimized infrastructure utilization and costs
      - label: Step 4
        title: Enable & Evolve
        content: We help your team adopt, operate, and continuously improve the platform long after implementation is complete.
        outcomes: |-
          - Comprehensive documentation and operational runbooks
          - Knowledge transfer and team enablement
          - Clear ownership and support processes
          - Ongoing platform optimization and improvement guidance
why:
  title: Why Our Process Works
  intro: |-
    We focus on measurable improvements, not assumptions. 

    Every step is designed to reduce risk, validate impact, and build confidence before making larger investments.
why_elements:
  - title: Impact First
    content: Every engagement starts by identifying the areas with the highest potential business and operational impact.
  - title: Proven Before Scaling
    content: Improvements are validated in practice before broader rollout, reducing implementation risk.
  - title: Designed for Sustainable Operations
    content: We focus on creating platforms that are easier to deploy, monitor, and operate over time.
faq:
  title: FAQ
  intro: Curious to know more? Schedule a call and get all your questions answered!
  cta:
    label: Let’s talk
    target: https://thescalableway.com/contact/
  items:
    - title: How much of our team's time does this require?
      content: Very little. The Assessment typically requires 2-3 hours with a technical owner, plus access to relevant systems and architecture documentation. Most of the work happens independently, without adding engineering overhead to your team.
    - title: Will this require changes to our existing stack?
      content: Usually not. Most engagements focus on improving reliability, deployment workflows, observability, and operational processes within your existing ecosystem. The goal is to make the platform easier to operate, not replace tools unnecessarily.
    - title: What happens during the Assessment and Proof of Concept?
      content: |-
        The Assessment identifies operational risks, inefficiencies, and optimization opportunities across your platform.

        The Proof of Concept validates a high-impact improvement in a controlled scope, providing measurable results before broader implementation.
    - title: How is it different from hiring more data engineers?
      content: |-
        More engineers don’t automatically improve delivery if the platform itself is difficult to operate.

        We focus on removing operational bottlenecks that consume engineering capacity, so your team can spend more time delivering value and less time fixing.
    - title: What happens after Phase 1?
      content: |-
        You receive a clear assessment of your platform, a validated improvement, and the evidence needed to decide on next steps.

        From there, you can proceed with implementation, expand the scope, or take ownership internally.
    - title: We already have orchestration, CI/CD, and monitoring. What would be different?
      content: |-
        Most teams already have these capabilities in some form. 

        The challenge is usually how they work together in practice. We focus on improving reliability, deployment safety, observability, and operational predictability across the platform.
blog:
  title: Our Insights
  intro: Selected Articles. Check our blog for more.
bodyClass: process
permalink: /our-process/index.html
layout: base
---

<header class="section page-header">
  {% svg "divider/soft-top-bubble", null, "seperator small" %}

  {% if hero.image %}
    {% image hero.image, "", null, "eager" %}
  {% endif %}

  <div class="section__inner region region-space-xl">
    <div class="wrapper flow">
      <h1>{{ hero.title }}</h1>
      {{ hero.subtitle | markdownFormat | safe }}
      <a href="{{ hero.button_target }}" class="button flow-space-l no-indicator">
        {{ hero.button_text }} {% svg "misc/arrow" %}</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="intro | wrapper">
  <header class="header | region flow prose">
    <h2 class="text-step-3">{{ intro.title1 }} <span>{{ intro.title2 }}</span></h2>
    {{ intro.content | markdownFormat | safe }}
  </header>
</div>

<div class="what | wrapper">
  <article class="feature region  grid" data-layout="50-50">
    <div class="flow">
      <h2 class="text-step-2">{{ what_are.title }}</h2>
      {{ what_are.content | markdownFormat | safe }}
      <a href="{{ what_are.button_target }}" class="button flow-space-l no-indicator" data-ghost-button>
        {{ what_are.button_text }} {% svg "misc/arrow" %}</a
      >
    </div>
    {% image what_are.image | replace("/src", ""), what_are.image_alt %}
  </article>
</div>

<section class="steps | wrapper region" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
  <div class="feature">
    <header id="steps-title" class="header | flow">
      <h2 class="text-step-3">{{ steps.title }}</h2>
      <p>{{ steps.intro }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="tabs mt-xl">
      <nav aria-label="Process Stages">
        <ul class="arrows | repel" role="list">
          {% for stageKey, stage in steps_elements %}
            <li>
              <h3><span>{{ stage.label }}</span> {{ stage.name }}</h3>
              <ul class="cluster" role="tablist">
                {% for step in stage.steps %}
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">{{ step.label.slice(5) }}</span>
                    <button
                      id="tab-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
                      role="tab"
                      data-tab-target="panel-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
                      aria-controls="panel-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
                      aria-selected="{% if loop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                      class="button"
                    >
                      <span class="step-title">{{ step.title }}</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </nav>

      {% for stageKey, stage in steps_elements %}
        {% for step in stage.steps %}
          <div
            tabindex="0"
            id="panel-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
            role="tabpanel"
            data-tab-panel="panel-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
            aria-labelledby="tab-{{ stageKey }}-{{ loop.index }}"
          >
            <div class="sidebar mt-xl">
              <header class="flow">
                <p class="button" data-label>{{ stage.label }} {{ stage.name }}</p>
                <h3 class="flow-space-2xs">{{ step.title }}</h3>
              </header>
              <article class="flow prose">
                <h4>{{ steps.title_what }}</h4>
                {{ step.content | markdownFormat | safe }}
                <h4>{{ steps.title_outcomes }}</h4>
                {{ step.outcomes | markdownFormat | safe }}
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>


<div class="why | wrapper">
  <article class="full region flow">
    <header class="header | flow">
      <h2 class="text-step-3">{{ why.title }}</h2>
      <p>{{ why.intro }}</p>
    </header>
    <div class="split mt-xl">
      {% svg "brand/check" %}
      <ol class="timeline">
        {% for key in why_elements %}
          <li>
            <span>{{ loop.index }}</span>
            <div class="flow flow-space-3xs">
              <h3 class="text-step-1">{{ key.title }}</h3>
              <p>{{ key.content }}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<div class="faq | wrapper region">
  <div class="sidebar feature">
    <div class="flow">
      <h2>{{ faq.title }}</h2>
      <p>{{ faq.intro }}</p>
      <a href="{{ faq.cta.target }}" class="button flow-space-l no-indicator" data-button-variant="blue">
        {{ faq.cta.label }} {% svg "misc/arrow" %}</a
      >
    </div>
    <div class="details flow">
      <div class="control | cluster" aria-label="{{ meta.details.aria }}">
        <button id="expandAll" class="button" data-small-button>{{ meta.details.expand }}</button>
        <button id="collapseAll" class="button" data-small-button>{{ meta.details.collapse }}</button>
      </div>
      {%- for item in faq.items -%}
        <details id="{{ item.title | slugify }}" class="prose">
          <summary>{{ item.title }}</summary>
          {{- item.content | markdownFormat | safe -}}
        </details>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrapper">
  <section class="full | region">
    <div class="wrapper flow prose">
      <h2><a class="no-underline hover:underline" href="/insights/">{{ blog.title }}</a></h2>

      {% if blog.intro %}
        <p>{{ blog.intro }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="grid gutter-s">

          {% set itemList = collections.allPosts %}
          {% asyncEach item in itemList.slice(0, 3) %}
          {% set headingLevel = "h3" %}
            {% include "partials/card-blog.njk" %}
          {% endeach %}

         </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

{%- css "local" -%}
  {%- include 'css/process.css' -%}
  {%- include "css/page-header.css" -%}
  {%- include "css/details.css" -%}
{%- endcss -%}

{% js "defer" %}
  {% include "scripts/details.js" %}
  {% include "scripts/tabs.js" %}
{% endjs %}
